    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474">

                <pb facs="0832" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg736"/>

                <head>No. 472.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 25,
                        1874</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 90.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit a copy of dispatch No. 161, of
                    the 10th instant, addressed to this Department by Mr. Thomas F. Wilson, the
                    consul of the United States at Matamoras. From this paper it appears that the
                    arrest of one Alexander D. Hamilton, charged with a crime for which, pursuant to
                    the treaty with Mexico, his extradition may be required, has been <pb
                        facs="0833" n="737" xml:id="pg737"/> prevented by the interference of
                    General Cortina in his favor. You will lose no time in making a representation
                    to the Mexican government on this subject, and will state that it is expected
                    such orders will be given to General Cortina as will allow the treaty to be
                    carried into effect according to its terms.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d474-a1.xml" xpointer="d474-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
